 </div>
 <div class="page-nav"><span class="page-info">Page 3 of 3</span><div class="page-links"><a href="/city-of-wonders?page=2#content" class="page-prev">&#8592; Previous</a><span class="page-next disabled">Next &#8594;</span></div></div>
 <div class="story-body" id="content">
  <p>They had understood that a city is a conversation, and they had made their city into a conversation that outlasted them. That is what the City of Wonders is: not a ruin, not a preservation, not a monument. A conversation that decided not to end.</p>
<p>Yuen filed her single-page report and did not request another expedition. There was no need. She had said what needed to be said. She had become, without fully intending it, part of the answer to a question that had been waiting for three hundred years.</p>
<p>Somewhere, in the valley that older records called the Cradle, the tower held its shape. The figures held their places. The device on the observation deck held its inscription, its smooth surface catching the light in ways no known material could manage.</p>
<p>And in the silence — the particular, textured silence of a place that has learned to wait — something continued to pay attention.</p>
<p>Something that had been the City of Wonders all along.</p>
<p>Something that understood, now, that it was no longer alone in the question.</p>
<p><em>End of story.</em></p>
